  chapter: "Congenital Heart Disease (Cyanotic)",
  level: "Moderate",
  q: "A term neonate develops severe, intractable cyanosis within 4 hours of birth that does not improve with 100% supplemental oxygen. Echocardiography confirms the aorta arises from the right ventricle and the pulmonary artery arises from the left ventricle. In addition to a balloon atrial septostomy, what pharmacological intervention must be initiated immediately to ensure survival prior to definitive surgery?",
