  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (ASD):</strong> Presents with a wide, fixed split S2 and a systolic ejection murmur at the left upper sternal border due to increased flow across the pulmonary valve, not a harsh pansystolic murmur.<br>• <strong>Option C (PDA):</strong> Presents with a continuous 'machinery' murmur best heard at the left infraclavicular area.<br>• <strong>Option D (Coarctation of the Aorta):</strong> Presents with absent or delayed femoral pulses, upper extremity hypertension, and a systolic murmur radiating to the interscapular back."
