  exp: "In Supracardiac Total Anomalous Pulmonary Venous Return (TAPVR), the pulmonary veins fail to connect to the left atrium and instead drain into a common pulmonary vein, which then drains into an ascending vertical vein, to the innominate vein, and finally into the superior vena cava. The enlarged vertical vein, innominate vein, and SVC form the 'head' of the snowman on chest X-ray, while the enlarged right atrium/ventricle form the 'body'. An ASD is mandatory for survival to allow oxygenated blood to reach the left heart.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Truncus Arteriosus):</strong> A single great vessel arises from the heart, overriding a VSD. Chest X-ray may show a right aortic arch but not a snowman appearance.<br>• <strong>Option B (Tricuspid Atresia):</strong> Complete absence of the tricuspid valve with a hypoplastic right ventricle. ECG classically shows left axis deviation (unique for cyanotic CHD).<br>• <strong>Option C (Ebstein Anomaly):</strong> Downward displacement of the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle, causing severe tricuspid regurgitation. Chest X-ray shows massive cardiomegaly ('box-shaped' heart)."
