  exp: "Hirschsprung Disease (Congenital Aganglionic Megacolon) is caused by the failure of neural crest cells to migrate caudally along the intestinal tract during embryogenesis. This results in an absence of parasympathetic ganglion cells (Auerbach's and Meissner's plexuses) in the distal colon and rectum. The aganglionic segment remains chronically contracted (narrow), while the normal proximal colon dilates massively, creating the 'transition zone'.",
