  q: "A 2-year-old boy presents to the emergency department with a large amount of painless, bright red blood per rectum. He is hemodynamically stable and has no abdominal pain, vomiting, or diarrhea. Physical examination is completely benign. What is the most sensitive diagnostic test to confirm the suspected anomaly?",
